codex
The current code has head attestations and threshold certificate checks, so the critique will not repeat the older verdict’s claim that those mechanisms are absent. The remaining gap is semantic: a signature attributes a head to an authority; it does not prove that the head represents a lawful history. The proposed replacement of the foreign-receipt premise with “the writer signs at most one head” fails for a writer that signs one fabricated head.

